{"assets":["/editorial-assets/bc069523d8f34c38c2135890074783f9739d56cde55144b259c3743c00981452.png","/editorial-assets/5698f9586a6b2cae693a220ca538f751b45aedc58f52c838ee67d86d28fefa12.png","/editorial-assets/0f08efbefe897a8342b7d8613146b37258b994e47af8ea2f3aeb247fb484e582.png","/editorial-assets/131ce51661be5c5f9cf3f74207b778d6a63705798519f07e8bd16b673040ab74.png","/editorial-assets/9da868919fa4eafb00ba5b3937648442c6f9570abcfa73635c5ab43b31ff76fd.png","/editorial-assets/0f5710b61e253aed60c8c06f8650cfdbdfe3c243130312d812ab2bcee15ad0db.png","/editorial-assets/fd60d511dc8fdd3a026967d7678d8b7b7c858d23d868fc9cc0f1a732bef4e292.png","/editorial-assets/e7f6fbe910a0cd1c4f4a7aa73d41820802b007be86e578bf8b1550ffb2741dad.png","/editorial-assets/1a2b35ef24c6eac1c89ea5ab7cd0129b683285f47d2957e14431818f10d35897.png"],"contestId":"888","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"problemCode":"888A"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/888/problem/A"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"888A - Local Extrema"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Iterate over indices from 2 to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1 and check if at least one of given local extremum conditions holds."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Overall complexity: "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":")."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"problem_section"},{"attrs":{"problemCode":"888B"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/888/problem/B"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"888B - Buggy Robot"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Consider the final cell after original path. It has some distance "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"dx"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" = 0 and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"dy"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"y"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" = 0. That means the path included at least "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"dx"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"dy"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" in corresponding directions. Let's remove just these minimal numbers of moves."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Finally, the answer will be "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"dx"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"dy"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", where ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"dx"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"dy"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") are distances from the final cell of the original path to (0, 0)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Overall complexity: "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":")."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"problem_section"},{"attrs":{"problemCode":"888C"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/888/problem/C"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"888C - K-Dominant Character"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"At first, notice that the final answer is minimum over answers for each character."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The answer for one character can be obtained like this. Write down lengths of segments between two consecutive occurrences of this character, from the first occurrence to the start of the string and from the last to the end of the string. Take maximum of these values. Answer will be this maximum + 1."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Overall complexity: "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"(|"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Alpha"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"|·"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":")."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"problem_section"},{"attrs":{"problemCode":"888D"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/888/problem/D"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"888D - Almost Identity Permutations"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's iterate on "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"m"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" — the number of indices such that "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" ≠ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". Obviously, 0 ≤ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"m"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" ≤ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"How to count the number of permutations with fixed "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"m"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"? First of all, we need to choose the indices that have the property "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" ≠ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" — there are "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/bc069523d8f34c38c2135890074783f9739d56cde55144b259c3743c00981452.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" ways to do this. Secondly, we need to construct a permutation "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"q"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" for chosen indices such that for every chosen index "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"q"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" ≠ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"; permutations with this property are called derangements, and the number of derangements of fixed size can be calculated using exhaustive search (since "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"m"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" ≤ 4)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"So the answer is "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/5698f9586a6b2cae693a220ca538f751b45aedc58f52c838ee67d86d28fefa12.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":", where "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"d"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"m"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") is the number of derangements of size "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"m"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"problem_section"},{"attrs":{"problemCode":"888E"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/888/problem/E"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"888E - Maximum Subsequence"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's consider the naive solution in "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"(2"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"superscript"},{"kind":"text","text":") or "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"(2"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"superscript"},{"kind":"text","text":"·"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"). Iterate over all subsets of original set, calculate sums and take maximum of them modulo "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"m"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Now we can use meet-in-the-middle technique to optimize it to "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/0f08efbefe897a8342b7d8613146b37258b994e47af8ea2f3aeb247fb484e582.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":". Preprocess the first "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/131ce51661be5c5f9cf3f74207b778d6a63705798519f07e8bd16b673040ab74.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" elements naively and push sums modulo "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"m"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" to some array. After this process the second half with following algorithm. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Take sum of the set and find the greatest total sum of current and some sum in the array. As any sum of two numbers less than "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"m"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" can go no greater than 2"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"m"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", we can consider just two values: the greatest number in array and the greatest number less than "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"m"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"currentSum"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" in the array. This can be found by binary search over sorted array."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Overall complexity: "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/0f08efbefe897a8342b7d8613146b37258b994e47af8ea2f3aeb247fb484e582.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"problem_section"},{"attrs":{"problemCode":"888F"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/888/problem/F"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"888F - Connecting Vertices"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"We can use dynamic programming to solve this problem, but we need to choose the states we maintain very carefully."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"One of the approaches might be: "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"dp"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"]["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"] — the number of ways to connect the vertices between "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" to vertices "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" or "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" if "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" are already connected (so there is no possibility to connect any vertex between "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" to some vertex outside)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"What "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"dp"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" values should we access if we, for example, try to connect "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th vertex to some vertex "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"? To get everything connected, we then have to connect vertices from interval ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") to these two, and vertices from ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" or "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" — and connections to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" from the second interval are difficult to handle. We need to somehow get rid of them, and the solution is to choose "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" as the vertex with greatest index that we connect directly to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". And vice versa, if we connect something to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", then we choose the smallest index of vertex to be connected with "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" directly."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"But that's not all we have to handle. Suppose we have four vertices, and 0 is already connected to 3. One of the possibilities to finish it is to connect 0 to 1 and 2 to 3, but if we process current dynamic programming as it is, we will count it twice (if we choose to connect 1 to 0 firstly, or if we connect 2 to 3). To get rid of this problem, we will use a flag that will denote whether we can connect anything to vertex "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", and if we choose to pick the first connection from "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", then we don't connect anything to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"So the solution is:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"dp"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"]["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"]["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"flag"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"] — the number of ways to connect the vertices from interval ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"flag"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" denotes if we can connect anything to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"How to calculate it:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":true},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" If "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" = "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" + 1, then "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"dp"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"]["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"]["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"flag"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"] = 1 (there is nothing left to connect); "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Otherwise set "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"dp"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"]["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"]["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"flag"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"] = 0; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" If "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"flag"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" = 1, then iterate on vertex "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" we connect to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and add "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"dp"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"]["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"]["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"flag"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"]·"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"dp"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"]["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"]["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"flag"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"]; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Iterate on vertex "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"y"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" we connect to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and add "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"dp"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"]["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"y"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"][0]·"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"dp"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"y"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"]["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"j"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"][1]. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The answer is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"dp"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"[0]["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"][0] (if vertices are 0-indexed). Vertex "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" is actually vertex 0, so don't forget to update the matrix "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" for it."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"problem_section"},{"attrs":{"problemCode":"888G"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/888/problem/G"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"888G - Xor-MST"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"We can use Boruvka's algorithm to solve this problem."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"This algorithm usually works in "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/9da868919fa4eafb00ba5b3937648442c6f9570abcfa73635c5ab43b31ff76fd.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":": initially MST is empty, and then we run a number of iterations. During each iteration we find connected components in the graph formed by already added edges, and for each component we find the shortest edge that leads out of this component. Then we add the edges we found to the MST (but we should be careful to avoid adding edges that form cycles in MST). The number of iterations is at most "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/0f5710b61e253aed60c8c06f8650cfdbdfe3c243130312d812ab2bcee15ad0db.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":", and each of iterations can be done in "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"m"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":")."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"However, in this problem we need to speed up this algorithm. We can do each iteration in "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/fd60d511dc8fdd3a026967d7678d8b7b7c858d23d868fc9cc0f1a732bef4e292.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" time using a binary trie. We can store all values from "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" in a trie. When we need to find the shortest edge that connects some component with vertices outside of it, we firstly remove all values contained in this component from the trie. After that, for each vertex in the component we can find the closest vertex outside the component in "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/e7f6fbe910a0cd1c4f4a7aa73d41820802b007be86e578bf8b1550ffb2741dad.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" by descending the trie. And then we insert the values of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" belonging to the component back into the trie. Since for each vertex we descend the trie three times (to remove it, to find closest vertex and to add it back), each iteration requries "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/fd60d511dc8fdd3a026967d7678d8b7b7c858d23d868fc9cc0f1a732bef4e292.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":", and the whole algorithm works in "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/editorial-assets/1a2b35ef24c6eac1c89ea5ab7cd0129b683285f47d2957e14431818f10d35897.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" time."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"problem_section"}],"kind":"document"},"schema":2,"sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/blog/entry/55701"}